# Cloudflare Pages redirects for the hugr site.
#
# Tested against the live domain on 25 September. The per-path rules that used
# to sit here (/privacy, /support, /waitlist, /download, /card, /fr) were NOT
# doing what they say: Cloudflare answered each of them with a 308 to "/", so
# byhugr.io/privacy landed on the homepage instead of the policy. They are gone.
# Only the catch-all below was ever doing the work, and it does it correctly:
# it serves the single-page app, whose router reads the path and shows the
# matching page (/privacy, /support, /waitlist, /download, /card).
#
# /fr/ resolves on its own, because fr/index.html is a real file.
# The /fr/* rule is kept so French deep links can be re-tested now that the
# rules above it are out of the way; if /fr/privacy still answers in English
# after this deploy, the fix is a real file, not a rule.

/fr/*       /fr/index.html   200
/*          /index.html      200
